  "status_text": "The little path now forces two flips even inside a much bigger board. Lean checked this for any connected board with marked lines AB and BC and no line from A to C. The circuit must say whether the selected dots touch every line and, whenever they do, report whether exactly one end of each marked line is selected. For n dots it needs at least n plus three gates, at least n plus one AND or OR gates, and at least two NOTs. Constants are free and gates read at most two earlier wires (L-lib-1208).",
